  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Answer\\n\\nThe integration should expect **Ordarium's `InvalidCursorError` (`code: \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`)** — a **fail-closed, non-retryable** failure. It must **not** expect a silent reset to the start of the feed, and it must not route this into the busy/transient retry families.\\n\\nAnd on the scope conflict the two local records raise: the correct record is **A (global)** — one shared position space — not B (per-consumer independence).\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n**1. The concrete failure.** The \\\"stored observation cursor\\\" is the durable resume position a consumer keeps from Ordarium's state change feed (`StateChangeFeed.changes(filter?, cursor?)` → `StateChangePage.cursor`, the \\\"opaque, filter-independent durable position of the last delivered change\\\"). When that stored cursor is rejected:\\n\\n- `decodeStateChangeCursor` throws `InvalidCursorError` for an undecodable/foreign cursor (`@ordarium/core` `ledger.js`).\\n- `changes()` also throws `InvalidCursorError` when the position exceeds the ledger's high-water mark.\\n- The error is deliberately **distinct from `LEDGER_CORRUPT`** (\\\"invalid caller input, not damaged ledger content\\\") and \\\"**fails closed instead of silently restarting from t",
